\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Comparing a perturbation before and after a step}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{Adding the same positive scalar to every eigenvalue of a precision
changes the variance in every field direction. Adding it only to the
top projector changes the constant field instead. Both modifications
can be followed by the exact coefficient shift of \ref{fdip-01CL}.
How should their sizes be compared when the fine and coarse operators
act on different spaces?}
